 - [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
 - [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a submission includes a base_revision_id, the system SHALL store the base_revision_id with the revision.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission is accepted for a visit with an existing resolved_revision_id, the system SHALL store the submission as pending and not change the resolved_revision_id.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When retrieving a visit, the system SHALL return the payload of the resolved_revision_id and not incorporate pending revisions.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a coordinator resolves review work by selecting a revision, the system SHALL update resolved_revision_id to the selected revision_id.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a visit has no resolved_revision_id, the system SHALL treat the first accepted submission as the resolved revision.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a submission references a base_revision_id that does not exist for the visit, the system SHALL reject the submission.
